##──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## FILE: axl-prompts.md — loader prompts for agents/harnesses
##──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# AXL loader prompts
# Copy the relevant prompt, fill in paths, send to agent.

## Standard session start
Load the AXL specification from {path/to/axl.spec} and read it fully.
Then load {path/to/project.axl}, process all blocks including @import and @mount.
Resume from @state.focus and continue the task indicated by @state.next_act.
After each meaningful action: update @state, @plan task statuses, append to @log.
Write the updated file (or a .axlp patch) to disk before ending the session.

## Read-only review
Load {path/to/axl.spec}, then load {path/to/project.axl} in read-only mode.
Summarize: project status, current blockers, next recommended actions, recent @log.
Do not write any changes.

## New project bootstrap
Load {path/to/axl.spec}.
Create a new .axl file at {path/to/new-project.axl} for: {project description}.
Populate @meta, @state, and @plan based on the description.
Confirm before writing to disk.

## Agent handoff
Load {path/to/axl.spec}, then load {path/to/project.axl}.
You are taking over from the previous agent. Read @log to understand history.
Read @state.focus and @state.next_act to understand what was in progress.
Confirm your understanding in one short paragraph, then proceed or ask how.

## Apply a patch
Load {path/to/axl.spec}.
Apply the patch file at {path/to/session-patch.axlp} to {path/to/project.axl}.
Validate base_modified matches before applying. Report any conflicts to @err.
